# Separate C32 endpoint profiles

The new harness is `tuning/profile_trunk_endpoint.py.draft`. It is runnable in place; activation is optional. It does not compile or install anything. Root owns the GPU runs.

CPU validation completed: 14 unit tests passed, CLI help succeeded, and static `cuobjdump` symbol selection succeeded against the installed v29 binary, SHA256 `54efa3f7bfe3410d3c2320b6494f50262cbb0dd60ae0a5579dabeaf0a2ea8e49`. No GPU execution or NCU collection was performed during this handoff. An independent source review found no stream, lifetime, mapping, or profiling-scope blocker.

Run the two commands sequentially from `D:\Research\DLSSNR-PyTorch` while the GPU is available:

```powershell
& 'C:/Users/Administrator/miniforge3/envs/meanvc2/python.exe' -X utf8 tuning/profile_trunk_endpoint.py.draft --endpoint plane --ncu 'C:/Program Files/NVIDIA Corporation/Nsight Compute 2026.3.0/ncu.bat'
& 'C:/Users/Administrator/miniforge3/envs/meanvc2/python.exe' -X utf8 tuning/profile_trunk_endpoint.py.draft --endpoint tile --ncu 'C:/Program Files/NVIDIA Corporation/Nsight Compute 2026.3.0/ncu.bat'
```

Defaults are B1/H1088/W1920/C32, device 0, SM120 and seed 29071. The controller requires `cuobjdump` on PATH. Each command creates a fresh timestamped `profile/trunk-endpoint-...` directory, preserving the binary, active CUDA/Python sources, both commands and report evidence. Keep source and binary unchanged through both collections; the harness rejects drift. `--worker` is an internal controller command, requiring the expected hashes.

Each run selects exactly one mangled entry point:

| Endpoint | Private operator | Selected symbol |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Plane input | `_inference_trunk_plane_to_bhwc` | `_ZN6dlssnr14trunk_endpoint13plane_to_bhwcEPK5uint4PS1_ii` |
| Tiled output | `_inference_trunk_bhwc_to_tile` | `_ZN6dlssnr14trunk_endpoint12bhwc_to_tileEPK5uint4PS1_ii` |

The full collection requests available `PmSampling` and `PmSampling_WarpStates` sections. The second collection requests source counters. Both use an anchored exact mangled-name filter, `--profile-from-start off`, one launch, kernel replay, and `--cache-control all`. Only a single selected conversion lies between `cudaProfilerStart/Stop`. The source report, PC stall correlations, rule-engine results, PM instances, typed metrics and exact selected-function SASS are retained. Unavailable PM sections or throughput counters are recorded explicitly.

The plane fixture scatters deterministic logical BHWC bytes using the retained original `down_offsets` formula. Its output must reproduce those logical bytes. The tiled fixture uses the independent original `image_offsets` formula to construct the expected physical output. Neither oracle invokes the new endpoint kernel or its word/shuffle map. Inputs exercise arbitrary byte codes, including every possible FP8 bit representation, without converting them to floating point.

Both workers check eager results, input bytes and outer guards. Before profiling, they capture the selected endpoint, change the input three times, poison the retained output, explicitly replay, and compare against fresh independent expected bytes. Capture alone is never treated as execution. The tile endpoint always uses the same supplied, aligned, guarded preallocated output. The plane endpoint's output is allocated by its launcher; it has byte equality checks but no external output guards. All references, allocations for fixtures, graph checks and hashes are outside the profiler markers. Full/source workers must agree on binary, source, GPU/runtime metadata, shape, seed, map, input and output hashes.

Read `analysis/full_typed_summary.json` for the numeric sustained-throughput metrics and their units, and the raw `*_metrics.json` files for all collected data. The existing analyzer's DRAM/L2/tensor gate is applied separately to this single selected kernel. High hit rate or occupancy cannot satisfy the 85% requirement; strings, booleans, missing and nonfinite metrics do not count as evidence. Reported logical traffic is 66,846,720 input bytes plus the same output bytes; it is not a claim about measured DRAM traffic.

Cold-cache NCU duration is separate from the resident paired-adapter benchmark. These profiles establish neither a whole-trunk speedup nor a native DLL performance win. Analyze the two endpoint reports separately before deciding which conversion to change.

The CPU checks can be rerun without CUDA:

```powershell
& 'C:/Users/Administrator/miniforge3/envs/meanvc2/python.exe' -X utf8 tests/test_profile_trunk_endpoint_cpu.py.draft -v
```
